# The Dockerfile ends with `COPY . .`, so anything left here lands in the image.
#
# CI builds from a fresh checkout and therefore never had most of these, which is
# why the gap stayed invisible: it only affects builds run from a working tree —
# `docker compose build`, and `make image`, which pushes straight to ECR. Those
# are precisely the builds that carry a developer's real credentials.

# Secrets and local data. The reason this file exists: api/.env holds SECRET_KEY,
# ENCRYPTION_KEY and the provider API keys, and aether.db is a real database with
# real password hashes in it. Neither belongs in a layer that gets pushed.
.env
.env.*
*.db
*.sqlite3

# Local virtualenvs: hundreds of megabytes, built against a different Python than
# the image, and carrying their own copies of dependencies. Those shadow copies
# also show up in image vulnerability scans, so the scanner reports CVEs for
# packages the application never actually runs.
.venv/
venv/

# Caches and build artefacts — noise in the layer, and they invalidate the build
# cache on every local test run.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.vite/
.coverage
htmlcov/
